To remove a Helm chart release, use:

Shell
helm uninstall myapp

Verify it's removed:

Shell
helm list

If installed in a specific namespace:

Shell
helm uninstall myapp -n default
Remove the Kubernetes resources created by the chart

After uninstalling, check:

Shell
kubectl get all

or

Shell
kubectl get pods

The pods created by myapp should be gone.

Remove the chart folder from disk

If you also want to delete the chart files:

Shell
cd ..
rm -rf myapp

Verify:

Shell
ls
Useful commands

List Helm releases:

Shell
helm list -A

Remove release:

Shell
helm uninstall myapp

Delete chart directory:

Shell
rm -rf myapp

Check pods:

Shell
kubectl get pods

Since your release name is myapp, the command you'll most likely need is:

Shell
helm uninstall myapp

This removes the deployment, replica sets, pods, and services created by that Helm release.

